## Reproduction is not priority or formal verification

All universal statements in the theorem bank use analytic arguments. Computation catches convention and implementation mistakes in the indicated finite domains. These proofs have not been checked in a proof assistant. Rerunning a supplied independent implementation is different from authoring an independent checker; the registry labels both explicitly. Cross-comparison can share reference data even when code differs.

The original aggregate audit attempt was interrupted during its historical stage. The successful individual logs replace that execution route; they do not change the aggregate attempt to PASS. Original source snapshots remain unmodified. Selected copied data directories can include inherited outputs not overwritten by the listed scripts; only the registry and fresh logs identify fresh computations.

The final portable runner subsequently completed 21 explicit stages with all PASS in a fresh copy. This validates the delivered reproduction path and repeats existing checks; it does not inflate the 102 distinct named tests. Initial launcher interruptions remain recorded in E00/E23.
